---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import { brand } from "../brand/config";
---

<Base title="Terms" description="Plain-language terms of membership." canonicalPath="/terms/">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p>
        The full membership terms will be finalised before the paid launch, with appropriate
        Australian-facing legal review. The current waiting list does not create paid membership,
        does not require you to accept paid terms, and does not obligate you to any future purchase.
      </p>

      <h2>Plain-language preview of the acknowledgement</h2>
      <p>Before paid activation, every member will explicitly acknowledge that:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ordinary {brand.shortName} events are constructed;</li>
        <li>ordinary {brand.shortName} events are intended to be cancelled;</li>
        <li>members are not expected to attend ordinary events;</li>
        <li>
          {brand.shortName} characters and references may be fictional; the {brand.shortName}
          does not claim fictional characters, locations, or partnerships as real;
        </li>
        <li>
          AI and automation may assist personalisation within the rules the {brand.shortName} sets;
        </li>
        <li>human operators perform selected real-world tasks (print, sign, post, call, gift);</li>
        <li>optional services remain controllable and may be paused or revoked.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the {brand.shortName} agrees to</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Cancellation will happen before the date. Cancellation is not a failure; it is the
          product.
        </li>
        <li>Your data will be handled under the published privacy policy.</li>
        <li>
          You can leave at any time. Cancellation stops future personalisation and any
          already-scheduled work for the cancelled services.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the {brand.shortName} does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The {brand.shortName} does not claim fictional partnerships, endorsements, or real bookings.
        </li>
        <li>
          The {brand.shortName} does not charge per-event, per-RSVP, or per-cancellation.
        </li>
        <li>
          The {brand.shortName} does not lock you into an annual contract without explicit consent.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The full terms will be published here before the paid launch. <a href="/faq/"
          >Read the FAQ</a
        > for the most common questions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
